            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Samuel 21:10",
        "book": "2 Samuel",
        "chapter": 21,
        "verse": 10
      },
      {
        "text": "And it was told David what Rizpah the daughter of Aiah, the concubine of Saul, had done.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 11,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Samuel 21:11",
        "book": "2 Samuel",
        "chapter": 21,
        "verse": 11
      },
      {
        "text": "And David went and took the bones of Saul and the bones of Jonathan his son from the men of Jabesh-gilead, which had stolen them from the street of Beth-shan, where the Philistines had hanged them, when the Philistines had slain Saul in Gilboa:",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 12,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Samuel 21:12",
        "book": "2 Samuel",
        "chapter": 21,
        "verse": 12
      },
      {
        "text": "And he brought up from thence the bones of Saul and the bones of Jonathan his son; and they gathered the bones of them that were hanged.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 13,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Samuel 21:13",
        "book": "2 Samuel",
        "chapter": 21,
        "verse": 13
      },
      {
        "text": "And the bones of Saul and Jonathan his son buried they in the country of Benjamin in Zelah, in the sepulchre of Kish his father: and they performed all that the king commanded. And after that God was entreated for the land.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 14,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Samuel 21:14",
        "book": "2 Samuel",
        "chapter": 21,
        "verse": 14
      },
      {
        "text": "Moreover the Philistines had yet war again with Israel; and David went down, and his servants with him, and fought against the Philistines: and David waxed faint.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 15,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Samuel 21:15",
        "book": "2 Samuel",
        "chapter": 21,
        "verse": 15
      },
      {
        "text": "And Ishbi-benob, which was of the sons of the giant, the weight of whose spear weighed three hundred shekels of brass in weight, he being girded with a new sword, thought to have slain David.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 23,
            "end": 26
          },
          {
            "start": 79,
            "end": 86
          },
          {
            "start": 101,
            "end": 108
          },
          {
            "start": 156,
            "end": 162
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 16,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Samuel 21:16",
        "book": "2 Samuel",
        "chapter": 21,
        "verse": 16
      },
      {
        "text": "But Abishai the son of Zeruiah succoured him, and smote the Philistine, and killed him. Then the men of David sware unto him, saying, Thou shalt go no more out with us to battle, that thou quench not the light of Israel.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 31,
            "end": 40,
            "text": "HEB aided."
          },
          {
            "start": 145,
            "end": 147,
            "text": "2 Sam. 18:3 (3–4)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 17,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Samuel 21:17",
        "book": "2 Samuel",
        "chapter": 21,
        "verse": 17
      },
      {
        "text": "And it came to pass after this, that there was again a battle with the Philistines at Gob: then Sibbechai the Hushathite slew Saph, which was of the sons of the giant.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 55,
            "end": 61,
            "text": "1 Chr. 20:4 (4–8)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 138,
            "end": 141
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 18,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Samuel 21:18",
        "book": "2 Samuel",
        "chapter": 21,
        "verse": 18
      },
      {
        "text": "And there was again a battle in Gob with the Philistines, where Elhanan the son of Jaare-oregim, a Beth-lehemite, slew the brother of Goliath the Gittite, the staff of whose spear was like a weaver’s beam.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 159,
            "end": 164,
            "text": "1 Sam. 17:7."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 119,
            "end": 133
          },
          {
            "start": 180,
            "end": 183
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
